1
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:06,360
Get a doctor in here.

2
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:08,560
I don't care if they give me drugs or electric shocks.

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,680
Just make it all stop so I can finally rest.

4
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,080
What's going on between you and Mr. Ing?

5
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:12,960
Have you met him yet?

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,040
Instead of wasting your time on me,

7
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:16,880
you should be helping your brother.

8
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,480
What happened to P'Phet?

9
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:20,440
Quit Araya Group right now.

10
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:21,960
Thanks so much

11
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,200
for giving me all the love that wasn't even real.

12
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,840
From now on,

13
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,280
we're over.

14
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:29,560
P'Ing, wait...

15
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:31,800
-We can't end things like this. -Dammit.

16
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,120
Once this is settled,

17
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,040
I'll come back to you.

18
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,120
Financial interests?

19
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:47,840
I was actually hoping there would be some.

20
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:51,760
But the truth is,

21
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,360
he wouldn't even let me treat him to a meal.

22
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:57,080
My secretary got him a cup of coffee,

23
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:58,320
but he wouldn't even accept it.

24
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,920
He's an incredibly upright person.

25
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:04,080
You seem to be defending him now.

26
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:06,560
You think I'm defending him?

27
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,039
Truthfully, I find him rather annoying.

28
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:11,280
He's made my job much harder.

29
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:13,560
When I saw the news,

30
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,440
I could hardly believe it was him.

31
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,440
What's his angle here?

32
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,360
Or...

33
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,760
did we just have it all wrong?

34
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,440
What was that sound?

35
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:29,960
I'm really sorry,

36
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:32,160
but I have a meeting.

37
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:34,800
If you need any evidence

38
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:36,520
or anything else,

39
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:38,400
we are more than happy to help.

40
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:41,640
Okay.

41
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,200
Thank you, Mr. Tiwakorn,

42
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,000
for being so cooperative.

43
00:01:45,039 --> 00:01:45,720
Thank you, too.

44
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:47,400
-Thank you. -Thank you.

45
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,120
My pleasure. Thank you.

46
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,200
Let's go, Mr. Ing.

47
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:09,320
Yeah.

48
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:31,720
If it's not Ing, then who is it?

49
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:33,600
I think...

50
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:35,880
someone must have realized

51
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:37,040
that we'd suspect him,

52
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,640
so they tried to play us against each other.

53
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:43,520
Dad, P'Phet,

54
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,240
you can leave without me.

55
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:46,840
I think I've figured something out.

56
00:04:47,159 --> 00:04:48,240
I'm going to go check it out.

57
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:58,640
-Cheers. -May only good things come our way.

58
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:01,360
-Nothing but good news. -Good things are coming.

59
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,440
Ing,

60
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:08,560
how's the Pattaya project coming along?

61
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,880
Whether our dividends increase

62
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,720
depends on how this project goes, doesn't it?

63
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:13,800
Right.

64
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:14,680
So?

65
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,320
Yeah.

66
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,880
Hey, we can trust him.

67
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,280
There's nothing to worry about.

68
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:21,120
Yeah.

69
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:24,280
Exactly, you've always been the best.

70
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,600
Let's drink.

71
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:28,560
-Come on, drink up. -Alright.

72
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:35,720
I'll be right back.

73
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:36,760
Well, let's continue.

74
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:38,840
-Come on. -Have a seat.

75
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:39,960
Come here, sweetie.

76
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,159
-Let's drink. -Come on.

77
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:42,840
-Come on. -This is good.

78
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,320
P'Ing,

79
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:47,080
these oranges from Chiang Mai are really sweet.

80
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,960
Is this how you apologize?

81
00:05:52,159 --> 00:05:52,840
Yes.

82
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:54,560
I'm sorry,

83
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,159
and I'm also begging for my life.

84
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,800
Please don't take revenge on me.

85
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,040
I'm terrified.

86
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,720
Are you messing with me?

87
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:10,560
No.

88
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,120
Would you like to try some?

89
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,680
Happy New Year.

90
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,280
Ing, where are you going?

91
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,480
All the relatives are here together.

92
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,320
I'm visiting Grandpa.

93
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,280
Please, make yourselves at home.

94
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:32,840
Oh,

95
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,560
but I guess you already have.

96
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:43,600
-Come on. -Alright, everyone.

97
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,360
Let's drink.

98
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:45,760
Come on.

99
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,440
This is Itt's Wi-Fi name.

100
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:55,960
Try using this IP address.

101
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:59,840
His laptop is completely clean.

102
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:05,600
P'Phu, look for the browsing history

103
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:07,960
and the logins to foreign websites

104
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:09,400
that were deleted.

105
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,440
Can you find them?

106
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,960
Let me give it a try.

107
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:15,360
There was a record of access to the dark web.

108
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,560
It really was deleted.

109
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:23,760
Found it.

110
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,520
The transfer records are all tied to this one person.

111
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,600
It really is this person.

112
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:28,280
[Prepare the documents as agreed]

113
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:28,960
[and transfer the money accordingly.]

114
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:32,640
It was him all along.

115
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:50,240
Oh, Yok?

116
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:52,440
You should've told me you were coming this late.

117
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:53,760
I would've saved some food for you.

118
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,480
It was you who framed P'Phet,

119
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,880
wasn't it?

120
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,520
Yok, what the hell is wrong with you?

121
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:05,000
That offshore account

122
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,920
and the triple-encrypted money transfers...

123
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,800
I've traced them all.

124
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,440
Stop this, Itt.

125
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:16,760
You once told me you couldn't read me.

126
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,680
Well, now I can't read you, either.

127
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,560
Why did you frame my brother, Itt?

128
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,760
Are you even the same Itt I used to know?

129
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,120
What are you talking about?

130
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,440
I don't understand.

131
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:36,480
Where is P'Ing?

132
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:40,640
Why are you asking for him?

133
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:43,520
It's New Year's. He must be home.

134
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:46,960
He's not here.

135
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:49,760
And where is he?

136
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:51,960
You know what he's like.

137
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,680
Who'd dare meddle with where he goes or what he does?

138
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:57,280
Itt, who is it?

139
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,520
Oh, Yok?

140
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,160
What brings you here so late?

141
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,240
Are you here to see Itt?

142
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,480
I need to speak with P'Ing about something urgent.

143
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:06,760
Ing?

144
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:08,160
He isn't here.

145
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,640
He left for Grandpa's a while ago.

146
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:12,960
Thank you, ma'am.

147
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,840
Just stop, Itt.

148
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:28,560
Don't make things any worse.

149
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,960
Why did Yok say those things to you?

150
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,280
Oh, it's nothing, Mom.

151
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:40,800
You should go inside.

152
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,040
I'll be right behind you.

153
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,760
-Okay. -Go on.

154
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:04,200
Thanks, P'Phu.

155
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,720
I've got something else to take care of.

156
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,520
Please excuse me.

157
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:07,520
No problem.

158
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:08,920
Happy New Year.

159
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,320
Thank you.

160
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,200
Hello, P'Phet.

161
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,760
Any updates?

162
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:26,320
Itt is behind all of this.

163
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,560
P'Phu will send you the evidence right away.

164
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,400
I've already confronted him.

165
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,920
I think he'll back off now,

166
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:34,560
but if the investigation

167
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:36,080
hasn't been dropped in a few days,

168
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:38,360
we'll hand the evidence over to the authorities.

169
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,040
Was it really Itt all along?

170
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:42,560
The Adularaya family is quite a tangled mess.

171
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,080
Are you coming home now?

172
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:46,680
I still have something to take care of.

173
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:47,640
What is it?

174
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:49,240
Itt and I...

175
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:52,960
actually took over the Pattaya project.

176
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:53,880
What?

177
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:54,880
Why?

178
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:56,360
It's a long story.

179
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:58,160
I never meant

180
00:10:58,160 --> 00:10:59,960
to drag you into this mess.

181
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,480
I'm sorry.

182
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:04,640
So, that something you have to take care of,

183
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:05,840
what is it?

184
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:08,160
I'm going to see P'Ing

185
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,560
and apologize to him.

186
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:12,240
Go on, and be careful.

187
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,480
Don't worry about things here.

188
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,080
Oh?

189
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,280
Yok?

190
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:36,720
Grandpa,

191
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,200
is P'Ing here?

192
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:40,520
Ing?

193
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,440
He just dropped some things off

194
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,880
and stayed for a bit,

195
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,200
and then he left.

196
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,200
Did he tell you where he was heading?

197
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:51,480
He mentioned...

198
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,160
he had to sort out something about...

199
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:56,000
the Phuket project or whatever it's called.

200
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,200
Phuket?

201
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,240
Well, Grandpa, I have something to take care of.

202
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:04,560
I'll take my leave now.

203
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,960
Kids these days...

204
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,880
They come whenever they feel like it

205
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,000
and leave whenever they want.

206
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,400
[Phuket Land Purchase Agreement]

207
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,720
[Tiwakorn Adularaya]

208
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,160
Everything is ready.

209
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:03,800
Thank you very much.

210
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:04,640
Thank you.

211
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,280
Secretary Piang,

212
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,080
transfer the funds immediately.

213
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,400
Let's welcome this great project

214
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,440
for the New Year.

215
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,760
As for me,

216
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:23,720
I'm going to bed.

217
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:25,120
I woke up way too early.

218
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:26,800
Understood. I'll get right on it.

219
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:58,560
P'Ing, where are you?

220
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:29,440
[Secretary Piang]

221
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:37,240
Hello?

222
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,400
Mr. Ing,

223
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:40,640
the land in Phuket has been seized by court order.

224
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:42,440
Accounting just completed the transfer,

225
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:43,760
so our funds

226
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:46,200
have been frozen as well.

227
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:14,440
P'Yot...

228
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,520
I was just about to call you.

229
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:18,120
Is it about the land in Phuket?

230
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:19,040
You already know?

231
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:20,320
I just found out.

232
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,200
The company selling us this land

233
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:24,320
concealed its outstanding debts.

234
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:25,480
How were we supposed to know?

235
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:27,240
The moment we signed the contract,

236
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:28,560
the creditor company

237
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:29,880
suddenly showed up.

238
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:31,360
Who's taking responsibility for this?

239
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,720
And what happened to that company?

240
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,640
The current management had taken over the company

241
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:38,480
and knew nothing about the old debts.

242
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:40,840
They only found out when the creditors came knocking.

243
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:42,280
They're demanding...

244
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,240
two billion baht.

245
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:44,880
Two billion?

246
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:46,440
Hey, P'Yot.

247
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:48,440
This is a very big deal.

248
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:49,760
You really had no idea?

249
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:50,640
Ing,

250
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:53,600
if I knew, I'd have skipped town already.

251
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,720
I wouldn't be here talking to you.

252
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:56,560
Okay.

253
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:58,080
I'm sorry, P'Yot. I...

254
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,680
I'm just overwhelmed.

255
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:01,840
I get it.

256
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:04,760
Anyone would be frantic in a situation like this.

257
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:05,800
Let's talk.

258
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,680
We need to figure out how to fix this.

259
00:16:07,680 --> 00:16:09,160
I'll do everything I can.

260
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:12,200
P'Yot,

261
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:13,600
let's talk later.

262
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:14,880
I've got something to do.

263
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:15,960
I'll reschedule with you.

264
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,280
Mr. Ing...

265
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:22,960
The landowner's creditors...

266
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,320
have requested a meeting right now.

267
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:26,680
They're here?

268
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:27,840
Already?

269
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:28,560
Yes.

270
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:30,240
They've requested that you go alone

271
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:31,520
and not bring Mr. Yot.

272
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:40,800
Dammit.

273
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,640
Talk about perfect timing.

274
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,360
The moment I hung up, they showed up.

275
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:49,240
Who is pulling the strings here?

276
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:54,560
Excuse me.

277
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:14,400
Secretary Piang,

278
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:17,040
you can leave.

279
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:20,040
I can handle this.

280
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:41,520
Hi, P'Ing.

281
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,440
It's been a long time.

282
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:46,320
How have you been?

283
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:10,120
You've gotten pretty good at this, haven't you?

284
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:12,640
I didn't let you down, did I?

285
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:17,960
What the hell are you doing, Itt?

286
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:22,080
You said we were here to talk business with him.

287
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:27,120
[Notice of Penalty Fine]

288
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:28,200
[Araya Group Co., Ltd.]

289
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,560
[Penalty Amount: Two billion baht only]

290
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:33,200
Two billion?

291
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:34,800
Have you lost your mind?

292
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:36,840
Yok,

293
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:39,120
you should be happy.

294
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:42,840
After all, you have a share in this, too.

295
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:45,120
I backed out a long time ago.

296
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:47,440
So you've been lying to both him and me?

297
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:48,360
Hey.

298
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:51,600
If you are going to put on a show,

299
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:53,440
could you do it somewhere else?

300
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:55,960
You're wasting my damn time.

301
00:18:59,000 --> 00:18:59,760
P'Ing,

302
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:01,960
I didn't know anything about this.

303
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:05,360
Who do you think you are?

304
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:08,200
What right do you have to touch me?

305
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,640
-Let go. -P'Ing...

306
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:13,960
I said, let go.

307
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:19,680
I don't care what you two are fighting about.

308
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:21,640
The only person I care about is that jerk.

309
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:24,000
As for you, get the hell out.

310
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,800
I'll be waiting outside.

311
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,280
Impressive.

312
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:04,120
You spent all this time pretending to be a fool

313
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:06,480
and letting me walk all over you.

314
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:09,200
I have to hand it to you.

315
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:15,200
Just tell me what you want.

316
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,320
Aren't you mad at me?

317
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,040
Just say what you have to say.

318
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,680
I just want half the shares

319
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:37,720
in Araya Group.

320
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:46,680
Do you think your leverage

321
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:49,160
is worth half of my company?

322
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:52,160
Well, it's enough to put Araya Group at a loss

323
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:54,520
and leave it billions in debt.

324
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:58,360
But Araya Group doesn't belong only to me.

325
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:01,080
With what you're doing,

326
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:03,440
do you think our relatives will just sit back and watch?

327
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:05,560
I don't care.

328
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,320
Aside from Dad,

329
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:11,440
everyone else is on your side anyway, aren't they?

330
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:15,160
Even if you all lose everything and go bust,

331
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,320
I'll just laugh in your faces.

332
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:22,080
And do you really think that...

333
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:27,080
I'd be afraid of my company going bust?

334
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:29,520
What a pity.

335
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:33,000
After all those meals at my house,

336
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:35,240
not a single brain cell of yours has gotten any smarter.

337
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,760
What makes you think

338
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:40,320
I'd ever submit to you? You idiot.

339
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:41,680
Do you really think...

340
00:21:43,120 --> 00:21:44,800
I'd ever let you boss me around?

341
00:21:46,760 --> 00:21:47,520
Listen.

342
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:50,440
I'd rather...

343
00:21:52,560 --> 00:21:53,360
go down in flames

344
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:54,920
than ever submit to you.

345
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:57,800
Don't think your pathetic little scheme

346
00:21:57,840 --> 00:21:59,040
can bring me down.

347
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:00,840
This is just the appetizer.

348
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,760
The real show starts now.

349
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:05,640
I'm going to ruin you.

350
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:21,840
P'Ing...

351
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:25,760
You've made my life a living hell for so long.

352
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:37,280
P'Ing, hey...

353
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:39,200
I didn't know anything about the Phuket project.

354
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:41,000
Please hear me out.

355
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:43,360
He's been playing us this whole time.

356
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:45,600
It's not just the Pattaya and Phuket projects.

357
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:48,520
He was the one who framed P'Phet, too.

358
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:50,120
That's why I misunderstood everything.

359
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:52,560
Yeah?

360
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:56,200
P'Ing, I really want to help you.

361
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:01,520
So you think being lied to...

362
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:05,680
makes you some poor, helpless victim?

363
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:08,000
That's not what I meant.

364
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,160
P'Ing...

365
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:11,040
When you decided to back out,

366
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,320
why didn't you tell me right away?

367
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:17,040
I never thought

368
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:18,440
he'd go this far.

369
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:19,800
I was just afraid that

370
00:23:19,840 --> 00:23:21,120
if you knew the truth,

371
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:23,040
you'd never talk to me again.

372
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:28,960
I thought you were just a scumbag,

373
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:31,600
but now...

374
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,240
I've realized you're also incredibly stupid.

375
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:37,640
You're right.

376
00:23:38,160 --> 00:23:38,840
Fine,

377
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,760
I'll believe you

378
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:43,120
that you're Itt's victim, too.

379
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:46,560
After all, using debt as leverage

380
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:50,280
to force me to give up my shares

381
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:51,640
isn't how you operate.

382
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:55,160
Shares?

383
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:58,920
He's making you give up your shares?

384
00:23:59,440 --> 00:24:00,160
Yeah.

385
00:24:01,720 --> 00:24:03,520
This kind of dirty tactic

386
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:05,680
is beneath someone as conceited as you.

387
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:06,840
Oh...

388
00:24:08,120 --> 00:24:09,000
I see.

389
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:13,720
You probably think Itt's the poor victim here,

390
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:15,440
while I'm just...

391
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:17,360
some tyrant who abuses his power

392
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:19,240
and pushes everyone around.

393
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:22,880
So I guess...

394
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:24,280
I got what I deserved.

395
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:28,040
P'Ing, that's not what I'm thinking.

396
00:24:28,960 --> 00:24:31,040
Oh, it's not?

397
00:24:32,960 --> 00:24:33,960
Then what are you thinking?

398
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:38,840
And yet you still had the nerve to suspect me

399
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:41,600
of setting your brother up.

400
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:45,400
♪ We don't fit on your canvas ♪

401
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:48,880
♪ We burn it all to ashes now ♪

402
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:51,880
You lied to me.

403
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:55,600
You used me.

404
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:58,120
And then you suspected me.

405
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:04,560
Let me ask you something.

406
00:25:07,120 --> 00:25:08,520
Do you really think

407
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:11,240
we could ever go back to the way we were?

408
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:18,920
I've made myself perfectly clear.

409
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:22,240
You should know where you stand.

410
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:45,400
Let go.

411
00:25:46,360 --> 00:25:47,200
P'Ing...

412
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:51,040
Let go of me.

413
00:26:26,240 --> 00:26:27,880
Dammit.

414
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,720
Hello, Manager.

415
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:50,440
I'm sorry to call you on a day off.

416
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,440
Are you free right now?

417
00:26:54,960 --> 00:26:56,080
I'd like to discuss

418
00:26:56,080 --> 00:26:57,880
the loan for the Phuket project.

419
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:01,560
Thank you so much.

420
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:03,080
I'll see you then.

421
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:19,040
Stay strong, Ing.

422
00:27:21,040 --> 00:27:21,840
Save your strength

423
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:24,360
to tear those two brats apart.

424
00:27:27,520 --> 00:27:29,720
Leo, book a VIP room for me

425
00:27:29,760 --> 00:27:31,040
and have some good liquor ready.

426
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:41,920
Dad.

427
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:43,560
Oh, Itt. You're here?

428
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:44,320
Yes.

429
00:27:44,360 --> 00:27:45,920
I wanted to ask you something

430
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,440
about the Phuket project.

431
00:27:47,520 --> 00:27:48,680
How is it going?

432
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:50,720
I heard rumors from the board

433
00:27:50,760 --> 00:27:53,200
that your brother got scammed big time.

434
00:27:53,480 --> 00:27:54,960
He's likely to face massive losses.

435
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:56,280
Yes.

436
00:27:56,640 --> 00:27:58,600
Things really aren't looking good.

437
00:27:59,800 --> 00:28:01,240
It's true we got the land,

438
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:03,040
but it came with a lot of debt.

439
00:28:03,360 --> 00:28:04,400
And now...

440
00:28:05,120 --> 00:28:07,120
the creditors are demanding that he pay them

441
00:28:07,760 --> 00:28:08,960
two billion.

442
00:28:08,960 --> 00:28:11,000
What? Two billion?

443
00:28:12,360 --> 00:28:13,760
Did Ing tell you this?

444
00:28:15,120 --> 00:28:15,920
No.

445
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:18,440
I knew about this even before he did

446
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:21,320
because one of his creditors...

447
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:23,440
is me.

448
00:28:30,800 --> 00:28:33,160
But I have no use for that much money,

449
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:34,320
so I told him to hand over

450
00:28:34,360 --> 00:28:36,200
half of the company's shares instead.

451
00:28:38,560 --> 00:28:39,320
You...

452
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:43,440
Itt, how dare you?

453
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:53,080
Why are you so mad?

454
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,400
Even if he transfers the shares to me,

455
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:56,760
Araya Group

456
00:28:56,760 --> 00:28:58,480
still stays within the Adularaya family.

457
00:28:58,520 --> 00:28:59,880
You ungrateful son.

458
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:01,080
You absolute scoundrel.

459
00:29:01,080 --> 00:29:02,800
If you still see me as your dad,

460
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:04,840
stop this madness right now

461
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,960
and apologize to your brother.

462
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:10,440
You kept telling me how much you love and pity me,

463
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:12,600
but in the end, you're still taking his side.

464
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:16,560
This is about doing what's right.

465
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,280
I'm your dad.

466
00:29:18,320 --> 00:29:20,080
I can't just let you do terrible things like this.

467
00:29:20,520 --> 00:29:22,040
Put an end to all of this.

468
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:26,760
What if I don't want to?

469
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:29,880
You...

470
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:31,120
Itt.

471
00:29:38,600 --> 00:29:40,200
You ungrateful son.

472
00:29:40,480 --> 00:29:41,800
He's your brother.

473
00:29:41,840 --> 00:29:43,120
How could you do this?

474
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:44,480
Honey, don't hit him.

475
00:29:45,040 --> 00:29:46,040
I'm teaching him a lesson.

476
00:29:46,080 --> 00:29:47,160
This has nothing to do with you.

477
00:29:47,280 --> 00:29:49,400
If you want to hit him, hit me, too.

478
00:29:49,720 --> 00:29:50,560
Mom,

479
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:52,680
if he wants to hit me, let him.

480
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:54,560
But Dad,

481
00:29:55,280 --> 00:29:56,840
I will never back down on this.

482
00:29:58,320 --> 00:29:59,920
You two...

483
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:02,840
have been manipulating me with your tears all this time.

484
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:06,760
Get out of my face.

485
00:30:08,080 --> 00:30:09,200
Get out of my house.

486
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:14,440
Come on.

487
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:15,840
Let's go.

488
00:30:18,560 --> 00:30:19,800
How could this happen?

489
00:30:25,600 --> 00:30:26,600
How could you make such a big decision

490
00:30:26,640 --> 00:30:28,320
without talking to me first?

491
00:30:28,640 --> 00:30:29,520
You can't spring it on him like that.

492
00:30:29,560 --> 00:30:31,600
Are you trying to give your dad a heart attack?

493
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:33,760
This "dad" you're talking about...

494
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,080
Which one do you mean?

495
00:30:56,920 --> 00:31:01,560
♪ The red sun rose this morning ♪

496
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:06,840
♪ Dark skies pronounce your warning ♪

497
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:10,120
♪ Nowhere to run ♪

498
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:11,360
Hello?

499
00:31:11,920 --> 00:31:12,640
Where are you?

500
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:15,080
What's up?

501
00:31:15,320 --> 00:31:16,840
Send me your location. I'll pick you up.

502
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:23,000
♪ Hold on, the floor is caving ♪

503
00:31:23,160 --> 00:31:27,800
♪ Your walls turn into cages ♪

504
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:40,880
Hey.

505
00:31:42,600 --> 00:31:43,680
Are you sure

506
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:45,360
I don't need accident insurance before doing this?

507
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,080
If you don't say anything,

508
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:11,640
I won't know what you want.

509
00:32:48,640 --> 00:32:49,360
Ouch.

510
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:58,880
Who did this to you?

511
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:01,680
You belong to me.

512
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:03,640
You belong to me.

513
00:33:20,760 --> 00:33:23,120
Yeah, I'm yours.

514
00:33:27,720 --> 00:33:28,720
It's okay.

515
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:30,920
I'll help you.

516
00:33:44,840 --> 00:33:47,120
Hey, I told you to open the door.

517
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:49,320
Can't you hear me?

518
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:51,560
-Hey. -Yes. Coming.

519
00:33:51,560 --> 00:33:53,080
Dammit, no one can do anything right.

520
00:33:53,120 --> 00:33:54,000
Hurry up.

521
00:33:54,520 --> 00:33:55,280
Come on in.

522
00:33:55,320 --> 00:33:56,040
Dammit.

523
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:02,240
What were you doing?

524
00:34:02,280 --> 00:34:03,520
Didn't you hear me?

525
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:06,720
I... I was in the bathroom.

526
00:34:10,480 --> 00:34:11,239
Dammit.

527
00:34:28,080 --> 00:34:28,840
Get over here.

528
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:33,560
Sit down.

529
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:48,600
You're scared?

530
00:34:58,680 --> 00:34:59,840
My life...

531
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:03,840
is freaking pathetic, isn't it?

532
00:35:05,880 --> 00:35:07,800
Full of myself, thinking I was so smart.

533
00:35:10,280 --> 00:35:11,520
And look how it turned out.

534
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:13,920
I got stabbed in the back.

535
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,240
Itt,

536
00:35:17,680 --> 00:35:18,760
Pite, those jerks...

537
00:35:22,960 --> 00:35:24,280
And even Yok...

538
00:35:29,880 --> 00:35:31,960
No one gives a damn about me.

539
00:35:33,400 --> 00:35:35,120
They only care about what they can gain from me.

540
00:35:44,040 --> 00:35:45,240
Pathetic, right?

541
00:37:48,520 --> 00:37:50,280
This is what you call a sporty look.

542
00:37:50,320 --> 00:37:51,560
Take notes, student.

543
00:37:51,840 --> 00:37:52,720
And this...

544
00:37:53,760 --> 00:37:55,920
is a nerd who has no sense of style.

545
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:00,880
Isn't it hot?

546
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:02,200
Shut up.

547
00:38:03,160 --> 00:38:04,560
Everything I say

548
00:38:04,600 --> 00:38:05,760
is always right.

549
00:38:05,880 --> 00:38:06,720
Remember that.

550
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:07,880
Once you're in America,

551
00:38:07,880 --> 00:38:09,120
you have to look like a superstar boxer

552
00:38:09,160 --> 00:38:10,600
and be fashionable. Got it?

553
00:38:10,640 --> 00:38:11,640
You can't let them look down on you

554
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:13,040
for having no sense of style.

555
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:13,960
Okay?

556
00:38:21,960 --> 00:38:22,680
Okay.

557
00:38:22,840 --> 00:38:24,360
My fashion sense is always on point.

558
00:38:24,600 --> 00:38:26,120
No matter what look I go for,

559
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:27,320
it's always perfect.

560
00:38:27,720 --> 00:38:29,040
Just trust me. Here.

561
00:38:29,880 --> 00:38:30,720
Wear it.

562
00:39:35,920 --> 00:39:37,440
Feeling down or not, you still need to eat.

563
00:39:38,760 --> 00:39:39,880
Want some?

564
00:39:42,200 --> 00:39:43,320
Shall we go to the usual spot?

565
00:39:45,120 --> 00:39:46,400
I was just about to say that.

566
00:40:06,880 --> 00:40:08,200
These stairs never seemed this steep

567
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:09,640
when we were little.

568
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:11,520
Here.

569
00:40:12,520 --> 00:40:13,320
Thanks.

570
00:40:17,880 --> 00:40:20,320
How old were we when we last came up here

571
00:40:20,560 --> 00:40:21,640
to eat noodles together?

572
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:26,840
Probably around seven or eight.

573
00:40:29,920 --> 00:40:32,240
Instant noodles tasted so good back then

574
00:40:32,480 --> 00:40:34,040
because we couldn't let Mom know.

575
00:40:34,960 --> 00:40:37,280
Now that we can eat them whenever we want,

576
00:40:38,040 --> 00:40:39,720
they just don't seem to taste the same.

577
00:40:45,040 --> 00:40:45,840
P'Phet,

578
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:50,360
Dad must be really mad at me.

579
00:40:52,320 --> 00:40:53,640
That's the least of it.

580
00:40:54,760 --> 00:40:56,440
He's actually worried about you.

581
00:41:09,040 --> 00:41:10,120
It's all my fault.

582
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:13,560
I've had so much going on lately.

583
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:16,520
Everything is a mess.

584
00:41:17,960 --> 00:41:18,960
I'm sorry.

585
00:41:22,120 --> 00:41:24,040
What's done is done. Just let it go.

586
00:41:26,080 --> 00:41:26,960
But what about Itt?

587
00:41:27,480 --> 00:41:28,640
What actually happened?

588
00:41:36,080 --> 00:41:38,440
He's been feeding me lies since we were little.

589
00:41:38,920 --> 00:41:40,880
He said Ing was always picking on him

590
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:42,600
and hurting him.

591
00:41:44,400 --> 00:41:47,240
He said he wanted to use the Pattaya project

592
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:49,240
as security for himself and his mom

593
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:53,040
and as a chance to teach P'Ing a lesson,

594
00:41:55,400 --> 00:41:57,160
so I agreed to help him.

595
00:41:59,600 --> 00:42:00,440
No wonder.

596
00:42:01,280 --> 00:42:02,520
That's why you've stayed at Araya Group

597
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:03,600
all this time.

598
00:42:06,280 --> 00:42:07,320
You know what?

599
00:42:11,160 --> 00:42:12,640
The longer I stayed,

600
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:15,640
the more I realized P'Ing isn't a bad person.

601
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:20,320
That's why I backed out of Itt's plan,

602
00:42:21,600 --> 00:42:23,040
but I didn't tell P'Ing about it.

603
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:27,040
I thought it would be fine.

604
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:31,160
But who could've known?

605
00:42:32,440 --> 00:42:33,680
Itt rigged

606
00:42:33,720 --> 00:42:35,000
another project,

607
00:42:35,120 --> 00:42:37,440
which left Araya Group two billion in debt.

608
00:42:38,240 --> 00:42:39,440
Two billion?

609
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:41,520
Yes.

610
00:42:42,040 --> 00:42:43,040
Two billion.

611
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:45,720
P'Phet...

612
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:51,000
I've always thought

613
00:42:52,720 --> 00:42:53,840
that I was smart,

614
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:58,440
but now I've realized...

615
00:42:59,680 --> 00:43:00,840
I'm a complete idiot.

616
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:04,440
I tried explaining everything to P'Ing,

617
00:43:05,160 --> 00:43:06,640
but he wouldn't forgive me.

618
00:43:20,960 --> 00:43:22,120
Listen, Yok.

619
00:43:23,440 --> 00:43:24,960
Give him some time.

620
00:43:26,920 --> 00:43:29,320
The view from inside a room is different

621
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:30,840
from the one up on a rooftop.

622
00:43:43,440 --> 00:43:45,000
What you need to do right now

623
00:43:45,400 --> 00:43:47,600
isn't to figure out how to make him forgive you.

624
00:43:51,000 --> 00:43:52,720
It's to figure out what he needs

625
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:55,800
and what you can do to help him.

626
00:44:05,320 --> 00:44:05,960
Okay.

627
00:44:08,080 --> 00:44:09,920
Eat up. You need the brain food.

628
00:44:21,880 --> 00:44:22,840
I gotta go now.

629
00:44:24,800 --> 00:44:26,200
Wait until I finish.

630
00:44:26,240 --> 00:44:27,480
We can head down together.

631
00:44:31,080 --> 00:44:32,320
I'm going back to Pattaya.

632
00:44:33,080 --> 00:44:34,520
I've got work to do tomorrow.

633
00:44:35,800 --> 00:44:36,760
That's right.

634
00:44:37,320 --> 00:44:38,440
Should I drive you?

635
00:44:39,480 --> 00:44:40,440
No need.

636
00:44:41,480 --> 00:44:43,040
I'll be coming home often.

637
00:44:43,600 --> 00:44:45,560
You can come to me if you ever need anything.

638
00:44:49,440 --> 00:44:50,000
Here.

639
00:44:50,960 --> 00:44:52,240
Finish the rest for me.

640
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:54,400
I'm off.

641
00:45:18,200 --> 00:45:19,320
[I have all the evidence of you]

642
00:45:19,320 --> 00:45:20,400
[framing and filing a complaint against P'Phet.]

643
00:45:20,400 --> 00:45:21,600
[If you don't stop this now,]

644
00:45:21,600 --> 00:45:22,960
[I'll hand everything over to the DSI.]

645
00:46:05,520 --> 00:46:07,440
I forgot to tell you. We're not having dinner at home

646
00:46:07,480 --> 00:46:09,000
this New Year's.

647
00:46:09,480 --> 00:46:11,280
How much longer will you keep this from me?

648
00:46:11,400 --> 00:46:13,320
I won't let that homewrecker

649
00:46:13,520 --> 00:46:15,520
disrespect my mom ever again.

650
00:46:16,080 --> 00:46:17,800
Please have all the necessary paperwork

651
00:46:17,800 --> 00:46:18,800
ready for me to sign.

652
00:46:18,920 --> 00:46:20,120
I'm leaving today.

653
00:46:20,120 --> 00:46:20,800
P'Piang,

654
00:46:20,960 --> 00:46:21,800
where's P'Ing?

655
00:46:21,960 --> 00:46:23,400
I've been waiting for you

656
00:46:23,480 --> 00:46:24,400
to come home.

657
00:46:25,360 --> 00:46:26,080
Who do you think you are,

658
00:46:26,080 --> 00:46:27,320
messing with my boy?

659
00:46:27,480 --> 00:46:28,960
I've got proof that Itt framed P'Phet.

660
00:46:29,000 --> 00:46:30,560
What makes you think I'd trust you this time?

661
00:46:36,080 --> 00:46:39,200
[The UNCUT version of Fool in Love]

662
00:46:39,240 --> 00:46:42,400
[is exclusively available on iQIYI and iQ.com]
